Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spi-nor: allow independent SPL manufacturer selection

DM and the tiny NOR core otherwise inherit the complete proper JEDEC table,
which can cost several KiB in a constrained SPL. Add phase-specific options,
defaulting to the existing proper selections, and use them for the table
and tiny manufacturer helpers. Proper remains unchanged.

Keep the SR1+SR2 quad-enable helper available for XTX and Zbit even when
Winbond and Spansion are omitted from SPL. ZB25VQ128 (5e4018) uses SR2 bit 1,
read with 35h and written by 01h with two bytes, as does XT25F128B.

Upstream-Status: Pending

